title: '4. Read receipts: a mark per node, with a fingerprint.'
pid: 27fb19fb-ad3f-4688-865a-2c8476ff454e
body: |2-
  For each node one has dealt with, record its ID and a hash of what one
  saw (title, body, contains). A node is new when its hash differs from
  its mark. This is Jeff's "mark another's changes processed" and Ed's
  second wish, and the diff view's processed marks already work
  this way ('docs/diff-view.org', "Marks, fingerprints and the store").
  Partial reading comes free. The cost is the birth problem: an unmarked
  node is either new (then a fresh fork reports its whole subtree) or
  old (then a node added later, unmarked, is never reported). Receipts
  need a default for the nodes they do not mention.
